problem:
Problem description
- A manufacturing planning problem is given for a furniture factory that produces multiple product types indexed by $$p \in \mathcal{P}$$.
- The planning horizon is a single production period, so all decisions are made for one aggregate time window.
- For each product type $$p$$, the factory has a unit selling price $$s_p$$, a unit manufacturing cost $$c_p$$, and a unit warehouse-space requirement $$a_p$$.
- The unit profit for each product type is the difference between its selling price and its manufacturing cost.
- The factory has a total warehouse-space capacity of $$W$$.
- The factory must satisfy minimum required production quantities for selected product types, represented by lower-bound demand requirements $$\ell_p$$.
- The total number of units produced across all product types cannot exceed the overall production limit $$Q$$.
- The planning goal is to choose production quantities that maximize total profit while respecting all space and production restrictions.
- Required business constraints:
  - Production quantities must be nonnegative and represent feasible integer unit counts.
  - Total warehouse space used by all produced items must not exceed the available capacity $$W$$.
  - Production of each product type with a minimum requirement must meet or exceed its lower bound $$\ell_p$$.
  - The total number of units produced across all product types must not exceed the production limit $$Q$$.
  - The objective is to maximize total profit over all product types.
- A solution is represented by:
  - $$x_p$$: the number of units of product type $$p$$ to produce.
  - $$z$$: the resulting total profit of the production plan.

Input Format
{
  "products": {
    "description": "Set of product types indexed by $$p \\in \\mathcal{P}$$.",
    "size": "$$P$$"
  },
  "selling_price": {
    "description": "Unit selling price vector $$s_p$$ for each product type $$p \\in \\mathcal{P}$$.",
    "shape": "length $$P$$"
  },
  "unit_cost": {
    "description": "Unit manufacturing cost vector $$c_p$$ for each product type $$p \\in \\mathcal{P}$$.",
    "shape": "length $$P$$"
  },
  "space_requirement": {
    "description": "Unit warehouse-space requirement vector $$a_p$$ for each product type $$p \\in \\mathcal{P}$$.",
    "shape": "length $$P$$"
  },
  "minimum_production": {
    "description": "Minimum required production vector $$\\ell_p$$ for product types that have demand lower bounds.",
    "shape": "length $$P$$"
  },
  "warehouse_capacity": {
    "description": "Total available warehouse space $$W$$."
  },
  "production_limit": {
    "description": "Maximum total number of units allowed to be produced $$Q$$."
  }
}

Output Format
{
  "production_plan": {
    "description": "Integer production quantity vector $$x_p$$ giving how many units of each product type $$p \\in \\mathcal{P}$$ to produce.",
    "shape": "length $$P$$"
  },
  "total_profit": {
    "description": "Total profit value $$z$$ achieved by the production plan."
  }
}

Example(s)

Input 1
{
  "products": ["tables", "chairs", "bookshelves"],
  "selling_price": ["$$200$$", "$$50$$", "$$150$$"],
  "unit_cost": ["$$120$$", "$$20$$", "$$90$$"],
  "space_requirement": ["$$5$$", "$$2$$", "$$3$$"],
  "minimum_production": ["$$10$$", "$$0$$", "$$20$$"],
  "warehouse_capacity": "$$500$$",
  "production_limit": "$$200$$"
}
